Rate-limit the "branch delay!!" warning.

PR SCOPE: OUT. Log noise only, no behaviour change.

Requires: ee-tlb-fixes.patch  (it also touches R5900.cpp)

Taking an exception in a branch delay slot is rare for games, so cpuException()
logs every one. A demand-paged OS faults constantly and a fair share of those
land in delay slots: one BlackRhino boot emitted 28,942 of these, about 11% of
the log.

Rate-limited to 50 rather than silenced, so the diagnostic survives for the
games it was meant for. Same spamStop idiom ee-tlb-fixes.patch already uses in
RaiseAddressError.

--- a/pcsx2/R5900.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2/R5900.cpp
@@ -206,7 +206,11 @@
 		cpuRegs.CP0.n.Status.b.EXL = 1;
 		if (bd)
 		{
-			Console.Warning("branch delay!!");
+			// Rate-limited: an exception in a delay slot is rare for games but
+			// routine for a demand-paged OS, where it floods the log.
+			static int s_bdSpamStop = 0;
+			if (s_bdSpamStop++ < 50 || IsDevBuild)
+				Console.Warning("branch delay!! (%d)", s_bdSpamStop);
 			cpuRegs.CP0.n.EPC = cpuRegs.pc - 4;
 			cpuRegs.CP0.n.Cause |= 0x80000000;
 		}
